    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AmperePerGram</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">`Ampere per gram` is a practical unit to describe an (applied) current relative to the involved amount of material. This unit is often found in electrochemistry to standardize test conditions and compare various scales of investigated materials.

