  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#Site">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Site</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Occupied atomic site within a unit cell: the crystallographic position together with the atomic species residing at it, not a bare geometric coordinate. This reading is what the formal axioms assert (v0.3.2 wording clarification): hasSpecies is a subproperty of emmo:hasConstituent, whose domain is emmo:Object, so every Site is entailed to be an emmo:Object with its species as a constituent — coherent for an occupied site, but not for an empty coordinate triple. Vacancies are therefore not modelled as Site individuals. Requires (v0.3.0) at least one hasSpecies value, mirroring the pattern already used by CrystalBond and Species.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Thing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nebf2c24b56c54f78a91163c4577b18e4b11"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Site</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
