    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siunits#"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">SI unit for pressure.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Pascal</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pascal</emmo:EMMO_6dd685dd_1895_46e4_b227_be9f7d643c25>
    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Pa</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">SI unit for pressure.</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">The SI unit of pressure. The pascal is the standard pressure unit in the MKS metric system, equal to one newton per square meter or one "kilogram per meter per second per second." The unit is named for Blaise Pascal (1623-1662), French philosopher and mathematician, who was the first person to use a barometer to measure differences in altitude.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
  </rdf:Description>
