    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">MetricPerm</skos:prefLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A perm is a unit of permeance or "water vapor transmission" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The metric perm (not an SI unit) is defined as 1 gram of water vapor per day, per square meter, per millimeter of mercury.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Metric Perm</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">perm{Metric}</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">MetricPerm</rdfs:label>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/PERM_Metric</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A perm is a unit of permeance or "water vapor transmission" given a certain differential in partial pressures on either side of a material or membrane. The metric perm (not an SI unit) is defined as 1 gram of water vapor per day, per square meter, per millimeter of mercury.

