  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#Arcminute">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <schema:unitCode rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">D61</schema:unitCode>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">MinuteOfArc</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">ArcMinute</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minute_of_arc</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/ARCMIN</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Arcminute</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A minute of arc, arcminute, or minute arc (MOA), is a unit of angular measurement equal to one sixtieth (1/60) of one degree (circle/21,600), or π /10,800 radians. In turn, a second of arc or arcsecond is one sixtieth (1/60) of one minute of arc. Since one degree is defined as one three hundred and sixtieth (1/360) of a rotation, one minute of arc is 1/21,600 of a rotation.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd6cec6f81ae84ad2953881773eab9f5eb65"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd6cec6f81ae84ad2953881773eab9f5eb64"/>
