  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#InchPerSecond">
    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">[in_i].s-1</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">[in_i]/s</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The inch per second is a unit of speed or velocity. It expresses the distance in inches (in) traveled or displaced, divided by time in seconds (s, or sec). The equivalent SI unit is the metre per second. Abbreviations include in/s, in/sec, ips, and less frequently in s.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">InchPerSecond</rdfs:label>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Inch per Second</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The inch per second is a unit of speed or velocity. It expresses the distance in inches (in) traveled or displaced, divided by time in seconds (s, or sec). The equivalent SI unit is the metre per second. Abbreviations include in/s, in/sec, ips, and less frequently in s.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
