  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#MicroFarad">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The "microfarad" (symbolized μ F) is a unit of capacitance, equivalent to 0.000001 (10 to the -6th power) farad. The microfarad is a moderate unit of capacitance. In utility alternating-current (AC) and audio-frequency (AF) circuits, capacitors with values on the order of 1 μ F or more are common. At radio frequencies (RF), a smaller unit, the picofarad (pF), is often used.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8246541a_f1f6_4d03_8bd7_fc6b76d17375"/>
