  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#MicroCurie">
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/otherunits#"/>
    <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MicroCurie</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Another commonly used measure of radioactivity, the microcurie: 1 μCi = 3.7 × 10 disintegrations per second = 2.22 × 10 disintegrations per minute. A radiotherapy machine may have roughly 1000 Ci of a radioisotope such as caesium-137 or cobalt-60. This quantity of radioactivity can produce serious health effects with only a few minutes of close-range, un-shielded exposure. The typical human body contains roughly 0.1 μCi of naturally occurring potassium-40.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">MicroCurie</skos:altLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_9ff3bf8e_2168_406e_8251_1d158fc948ae"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd6cec6f81ae84ad2953881773eab9f5eb1960"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_515b5579_d526_4842_9e6f_ecc34db6f368"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="nd6cec6f81ae84ad2953881773eab9f5eb1959"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curie?oldid=495080313</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/MicroCi</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">μCi</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">uCi</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
    <skos:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MicroCurie</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">Another commonly used measure of radioactivity, the microcurie: 1 μCi = 3.7 × 10 disintegrations per second = 2.22 × 10 disintegrations per minute. A radiotherapy machine may have roughly 1000 Ci of a radioisotope such as caesium-137 or cobalt-60. This quantity of radioactivity can produce serious health effects with only a few minutes of close-range, un-shielded exposure. The typical human body contains roughly 0.1 μCi of naturally occurring potassium-40.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
  </rdf:Description>
