    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en"> (C/mol) is a unit in the category of Molar electric charge. It is also known as coulombs/mol. Coulomb Per Mol has a dimension of TN{-1}I where T is time, N is amount of substance, and I is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/C-PER-MOL</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">c/mol</emmo:EMMO_7f1dec83_d85e_4e1b_b7bd_c9442d4f5a64>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en"> (C/mol) is a unit in the category of Molar electric charge. It is also known as coulombs/mol. Coulomb Per Mol has a dimension of TN{-1}I where T is time, N is amount of substance, and I is electric current. This unit is the standard SI unit in this category.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Coulomb per Mole</skos:altLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
