    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The standard atmosphere (symbol: atm) is an international reference pressure defined as 101.325  kPa and formerly used as unit of pressure. For practical purposes it has been replaced by the bar which is 100 kPa. The difference of about 1% is not significant for many applications, and is within the error range of common pressure gauges.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Standard Atmosphere</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The standard atmosphere (symbol: atm) is an international reference pressure defined as 101.325  kPa and formerly used as unit of pressure. For practical purposes it has been replaced by the bar which is 100 kPa. The difference of about 1% is not significant for many applications, and is within the error range of common pressure gauges.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
