    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_f6070071_d054_4b17_9d2d_f446f7147d0f"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilowatt_hour?oldid=494927235</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siacceptedunits#"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">The kilowatt hour, or kilowatt-hour, (symbol kW · h, kW h or kWh) is a unit of energy equal to 1000 watt hours or 3.6 megajoules. For constant power, energy in watt hours is the product of power in watts and time in hours. The kilowatt hour is most commonly known as a billing unit for energy delivered to consumers by electric utilities.

-- QUDT</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <skos:prefLabel rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KiloWattHour</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The kilowatt hour, or kilowatt-hour, (symbol kW · h, kW h or kWh) is a unit of energy equal to 1000 watt hours or 3.6 megajoules. For constant power, energy in watt hours is the product of power in watts and time in hours. The kilowatt hour is most commonly known as a billing unit for energy delivered to consumers by electric utilities.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
    <emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">kW.h</emmo:EMMO_33ae2d07_5526_4555_a0b4_8f4c031b5652>
