  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#StructureFamily">
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Structural-prototype classification of a crystal structure (e.g. which well-known battery-material structure type it belongs to: layered oxide, olivine, spinel, garnet, sulfide superionic conductor, ...). New in v0.3.0. Confirmed absent from EMMO core, EMMO domain-battery, EMMO domain-electrochemistry, EMMO domain-chemical-substance, and EMMO's work-in-progress domain-crystallography ontology (v0.1.0, not imported here) — this branch is a genuine BattGPT extension, not a restatement of an upstream concept. It is deliberately the deepest local subclass hierarchy in the ontology: it is the intended conditioning vocabulary for hyperbolic (OnT) embedding and for CrystaLLM soft-prompt conditioning. A composite concept like 'Layered Oxide Cathode' is not given its own class; it is queried as a material with hasStructureFamily some LayeredOxideStructure and belongsToElectrode PositiveElectrodeRoleIndividual, which avoids a combinatorial explosion of family-x-role classes, most of which would never be populated.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">StructureFamily</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#"/>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">StructureFamily</rdfs:label>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Structural-prototype classification of a crystal structure.</skos:definition>
