  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8dd40ec6_2c5a_43f3_bf64_cadcd447a1c1">
    <emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&amp;ievref=113-04-38</emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">At a point fixed in a medium with a temperature field, scalar quantity λ characterizing the ability of the medium to transmit heat through a surface element containing that point: φ = −λ grad T, where φ is the density of heat flow rate and T is thermodynamic temperature.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">In an anisotropic medium, thermal conductivity is a tensor quantity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_2946d40b_24a1_47fa_8176_e3f79bb45064"/>
