    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A causal system possessing bonding that can not be represented by a simple Feynman diagram.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/chemistry#"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A causal system possessing bonding that can not be represented by a simple Feynman diagram.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A generic physical system is everything which is more complex than a scattering interaction, or a decay/annihilation event, which are represented by a single Feynman diagram.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_e7aac247_31d6_4b2e_9fd2_e842b1b7ccac"/>
