    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_15344998_4490_4b40_b242_c3d92e5cdc27"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/AT-PER-M</emmo:EMMO_1f1b164d_ec6a_4faa_8d5e_88bda62316cc>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The  `Ampere Turn per Metre` is the SI unit of magnetic field strength. One ampere per meter is equal to π/250 oersteds (12.566 371 millioersteds) in CGS units. The ampere per meter is also the SI unit of "magnetization" in the sense of magnetic dipole moment per unit volume; in this context 1 A/m = 0.001 emu per cubic centimeter.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
