  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_1e877c70_3b01_45a8_a8f6_8ce4f6a24660">
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Dedomena</skos:altLabel>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Pattern</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9 xml:lang="en">A perspective in which entities are represented according to the variation of their properties.</emmo:EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Contrast</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">A contrast is a causal object whose variations (non-uniformity) can be recognised and eventually interpreted.
A contrast can be of different physical types (e.g., matter, wave, atomic excited states).
How the variations are recognised and eventually decoded depends on the interpreting rules that characterise that type of contrast.
Variations are pure physical variations and do not necessarily possess semantic meaning.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f xml:lang="en">The covering axiom that defines the contrast class discriminates within all the possible causal objects between encoded contrast (data) or non encoded contrast.</emmo:EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A perspective in which entities are represented according to the variation of their properties.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Contrast</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_49267eba_5548_4163_8f36_518d65b583f9"/>
    <rdfs:seeAlso xml:lang="en">Luciano Floridi, "Information - A very Short Introduction", Oxford University Press., (2010) ISBN 978-0199551378</rdfs:seeAlso>
  </rdf:Description>
