    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    <emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilbert?oldid=492755037</emmo:EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The fundamental unit of magnetomotive force (mmf) in electromagnetic units is called a Gilbert. It is the mmf which will produce a magnetic field strength of one Gauss (Maxwell per Square Centimeter) in a path one centimeter long.

-- QUDT</rdfs:comment>
