  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_ee7ddcb8_ad8e_4ff7_a09f_889d8edf8f8b">
    <emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://www.electropedia.org/iev/iev.nsf/display?openform&amp;ievref=113-04-37</emmo:EMMO_50c298c2_55a2_4068_b3ac_4e948c33181f>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Vector quantity with magnitude equal to the heat flow rate dΦ through a surface element divided by the area dA of the element, and direction eφ in the direction of propagation of heat.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">At a fixed point in a medium, the direction of propagation of heat is opposite to the temperature gradient. At a point on the surface separating two media with different temperatures, the direction of propagation of heat is normal to the surface, from higher to lower temperatures.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">AreicHeatFlowRate</skos:altLabel>
    <emmo:EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1478382</emmo:EMMO_26bf1bef_d192_4da6_b0eb_d2209698fb54>
